# shadcn/ui Component Library Standards

This project uses **shadcn/ui** for all UI elements and components.

## Initialization

If shadcn/ui is not initialized in the project, use the following command:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Component Installation

If a particular component is not installed, use the following command pattern:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]
```

**Example:** To install the button component:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

## Standards

- **Always use shadcn/ui components** for UI elements instead of creating custom components from scratch
- Check if a component exists in shadcn/ui before implementing custom alternatives
- Follow shadcn/ui component patterns and conventions
- Use the official shadcn/ui installation commands to add new components to the project

## Common Components

Some frequently used shadcn/ui components include:
- `button` - Interactive buttons
- `card` - Content containers
- `input` - Form inputs
- `dialog` - Modal dialogs
- `toast` - Notification toasts
- `dropdown-menu` - Dropdown menus
- `select` - Select dropdowns
- `checkbox` - Checkboxes
- `radio-group` - Radio button groups
- `tabs` - Tab navigation